  "description": "Creates or updates an sbxenv.yaml, the Docker Sandboxes (sbx) environment file read by `sbx env plan|create|run|rm`. Inspects the working directory and suggests v3 kits from the live Docker Hub catalog (sbx and docker orgs), sets kit args and environment args, sets up credential bindings, secrets and registry credentials, and refreshes kit references to the highest version tags (and digests when pinned). Use when asked to create, write, scaffold, update, upgrade, bump, pin or review an sbxenv.yaml or ~/.sbxenv.yaml, or to set up a project for `sbx env`.",
